IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-part6`

-- Tests for wa-interpretation-part6.l4 (ss 40 to 47).  Expected values are written from the text.

§ `Tests -- Part VI`

-- s 40: the Governor makes it unless the written law says who.
#ASSERT `who makes the subsidiary legislation` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST "the Governor"
#ASSERT `who makes the subsidiary legislation` TRUE (JUST "the Minister") EQUALS JUST "the Minister"
#ASSERT `who makes the subsidiary legislation` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `who makes the subsidiary legislation` FALSE (JUST "the Minister") EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 41(1)(a): published in the Gazette or on the WA legislation website.
#ASSERT `the subsidiary legislation is published as section 41(1)(a) requires` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `the subsidiary legislation is published as section 41(1)(a) requires` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `the subsidiary legislation is published as section 41(1)(a) requires` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the subsidiary legislation is published as section 41(1)(a) requires` FALSE FALSE)

-- s 42(1): published Wednesday 5 March 2025.  Sitting days are 4 March (before), 5 March (the day itself, which
-- s 61(1)(a) leaves out), then 11, 12, 13, 18, 19, 20 and 25 March.  The sixth sitting day after the 5th is 20 March.
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`test sitting days around 5 March 2025` MEANS LIST (Date 4 3 2025), (Date 5 3 2025), (Date 11 3 2025), (Date 12 3 2025), (Date 13 3 2025), (Date 18 3 2025), (Date 19 3 2025), (Date 20 3 2025), (Date 25 3 2025)

#ASSERT `the last day for laying the regulations before the House` (Date 5 3 2025) (`test sitting days around 5 March 2025`) EQUALS JUST (Date 20 3 2025)
-- published on 3 March: the sitting days after it are 4, 5, 11, 12, 13 and 18 March, so the sixth is 18 March
-- (the first draft of this test said 13 March, a miscount by hand; recounted from the list here, and the code was right)
#ASSERT `the last day for laying the regulations before the House` (Date 3 3 2025) (`test sitting days around 5 March 2025`) EQUALS JUST (Date 18 3 2025)
-- fewer than six sitting days remain on the list: the answer is not yet known
#ASSERT `the last day for laying the regulations before the House` (Date 12 3 2025) (`test sitting days around 5 March 2025`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the last day for laying the regulations before the House` (Date 5 3 2025) EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 42(2) and (3): laid Tuesday 6 May 2025.  The 14th sitting day after it (not counting 6 May itself) is 5 June,
-- though the days fall in different weeks and the list could cross a recess.
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`test sitting days around 6 May 2025` MEANS LIST (Date 6 5 2025), (Date 7 5 2025), (Date 8 5 2025), (Date 13 5 2025), (Date 14 5 2025), (Date 15 5 2025), (Date 20 5 2025), (Date 21 5 2025), (Date 22 5 2025), (Date 27 5 2025), (Date 28 5 2025), (Date 29 5 2025), (Date 3 6 2025), (Date 4 6 2025), (Date 5 6 2025), (Date 10 6 2025)

#ASSERT `the last day for giving notice of a resolution disallowing the regulations` (Date 6 5 2025) (`test sitting days around 6 May 2025`) EQUALS JUST (Date 5 6 2025)
-- laid the day before: 6 May is then the first sitting day, so the 14th is 4 June
#ASSERT `the last day for giving notice of a resolution disallowing the regulations` (Date 5 5 2025) (`test sitting days around 6 May 2025`) EQUALS JUST (Date 4 6 2025)
-- laid on 8 May: only 12 sitting days follow it on the list
#ASSERT `the last day for giving notice of a resolution disallowing the regulations` (Date 29 5 2025) (`test sitting days around 6 May 2025`) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 42(2): the regulations cease to have effect on either ground.
#ASSERT `the regulations cease to have effect` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `the regulations cease to have effect` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `the regulations cease to have effect` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the regulations cease to have effect` FALSE FALSE)

-- s 42(2): validity of what was done in the meantime is neither affected nor cured.
#ASSERT `the thing done in the meantime is valid after the regulations cease to have effect` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the thing done in the meantime is valid after the regulations cease to have effect` FALSE)

-- s 42(4): 7 days from publication expire at the end of the 7th day after it; the regulations take effect the day after.
#ASSERT `the first day the amended or substituted regulations take effect` (Date 10 4 2025) EQUALS Date 18 4 2025
#ASSERT `the first day the amended or substituted regulations take effect` (Date 25 4 2025) EQUALS Date 3 5 2025
#ASSERT `the first day the amended or substituted regulations take effect` (Date 28 12 2025) EQUALS Date 5 1 2026

-- s 42(5): within 21 days of the passing.
#ASSERT `the last day for publishing notice of the resolution` (Date 10 2 2025) EQUALS Date 3 3 2025
#ASSERT `the last day for publishing notice of the resolution` (Date 20 12 2025) EQUALS Date 10 1 2026

-- s 42(6): revival.
#ASSERT `the first day the previous regulations are revived` `disallowed by a resolution` TRUE (Date 10 6 2025) (Date 20 3 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 10 6 2025)
#ASSERT `the first day the previous regulations are revived` `not laid in accordance with subsection (1)` TRUE (Date 10 6 2025) (Date 20 3 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 21 3 2025)
#ASSERT `the first day the previous regulations are revived` `disallowed by a resolution` FALSE (Date 10 6 2025) (Date 20 3 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the first day the previous regulations are revived` `not laid in accordance with subsection (1)` FALSE (Date 10 6 2025) (Date 20 3 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the day after the last day, across a month end
#ASSERT `the first day the previous regulations are revived` `not laid in accordance with subsection (1)` TRUE (Date 10 6 2025) (Date 31 3 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 4 2025)

-- s 42(7): regulations made by someone other than the Governor and needing confirmation.
#ASSERT NOT (`subsection (1) applies to the regulations` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `subsection (1) applies to the regulations` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `subsection (1) applies to the regulations` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `subsection (1) applies to the regulations` FALSE TRUE

-- s 42(8): regulations includes a regulation, part of one, rules, local laws and bylaws.
#ASSERT `section 42 treats it as regulations` `regulations` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `section 42 treats it as regulations` `a regulation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `section 42 treats it as regulations` `part of a regulation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `section 42 treats it as regulations` `rules` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `section 42 treats it as regulations` `local laws` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `section 42 treats it as regulations` `bylaws` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `section 42 treats it as regulations` `some other kind of subsidiary legislation` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 43(1) to (5).
#ASSERT `the subsidiary legislation is void to the extent of the inconsistency` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the subsidiary legislation is void to the extent of the inconsistency` FALSE)
#ASSERT `it is deemed to be made in exercise of the power` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `it is deemed to be made in exercise of the power` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`it is deemed to be made in exercise of the power` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `all conditions and preliminary steps precedent to making it are presumed complied with` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `all conditions and preliminary steps precedent to making it are presumed complied with` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power includes a power to amend or repeal the subsidiary legislation, in the like manner and on the like conditions` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the power includes a power to amend or repeal the subsidiary legislation, in the like manner and on the like conditions` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the listing of special purposes limits the power for the general purpose` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the listing of special purposes limits the power for the general purpose` FALSE)

-- s 43(6): a maximum fine of $1000, but only for enactments passed or made on or after 1 July 1984, and not for one
-- that merely continues or directly amends existing text (s 3(3)).
#ASSERT `the most a fine may be under regulations, rules, local laws or bylaws` (Date 1 7 1984) FALSE EQUALS JUST 1000
#ASSERT `the most a fine may be under regulations, rules, local laws or bylaws` (Date 1 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST 1000
#ASSERT `the most a fine may be under regulations, rules, local laws or bylaws` (Date 30 6 1984) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the most a fine may be under regulations, rules, local laws or bylaws` (Date 1 3 2025) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a fine is within the limit section 43(6) allows` 1000 (Date 1 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a fine is within the limit section 43(6) allows` 999 (Date 1 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a fine is within the limit section 43(6) allows` 1001 (Date 1 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a fine is within the limit section 43(6) allows` 1001 (Date 30 6 1984) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a fine is within the limit section 43(6) allows` 1001 (Date 1 3 2025) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 43(7) to (9): every way listed, and one that is not.
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised` `in relation to all cases to which the power extends` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised` `in relation to all those cases subject to specified exceptions` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised` `in relation to a specified case or class of case` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised` `the same provision for all cases` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised` `different provision for different cases or classes of case` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised` `different provisions for the same case or class of case for different purposes` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised` `unconditionally` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised` `subject to a specified condition` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised` `to apply at all times or at a specified time` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised` `to apply throughout the State or in a specified part of it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised` `to require a matter to be in accordance with a specified standard or requirement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised` `to require a matter to be approved by or to the satisfaction of a specified person or body or class` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised` `to confer a discretionary authority on a specified person or body or class` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised` `to exempt persons or things or a class, unconditionally or on conditions, wholly or to a specified extent` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised` `in some way not listed` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 43(9)
#ASSERT `it is specified for section 43(7) and (8)` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`it is specified for section 43(7) and (8)` FALSE)

-- s 44.
#ASSERT `the Act a reference in subsidiary legislation to the Act means` "Dog Act 1976" EQUALS "Dog Act 1976"
#ASSERT `the word has the same meaning as in the written law under which the subsidiary legislation is made` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the word has the same meaning as in the written law under which the subsidiary legislation is made` FALSE)

-- s 45(1) and (2).
#ASSERT `subsidiary legislation may provide for` `specific fees or charges` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `subsidiary legislation may provide for` `maximum or minimum fees or charges` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `subsidiary legislation may provide for` `maximum and minimum fees or charges` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `subsidiary legislation may provide for` `ad valorem fees or charges` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `subsidiary legislation may provide for` `payment generally or under specified conditions or in specified circumstances` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `subsidiary legislation may provide for` `reduction, waiver or refund, in whole or in part` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `subsidiary legislation may provide for` `some other provision about fees or charges` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a reduction, waiver or refund may be expressed to apply` `in respect of certain matters or transactions or classes of them` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a reduction, waiver or refund may be expressed to apply` `in respect of certain documents or classes of document` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a reduction, waiver or refund may be expressed to apply` `when any event happens or ceases to happen` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a reduction, waiver or refund may be expressed to apply` `in respect of certain persons or classes of person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a reduction, waiver or refund may be expressed to apply` `in respect of any combination of those` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a reduction, waiver or refund may be expressed to apply` `subject to conditions specified in the subsidiary legislation or in the discretion of a person it specifies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a reduction, waiver or refund may be expressed to apply` `in some other way` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 45A.
#ASSERT `expenditure is relevant to the scheme or system under which the licence is issued` `expenditure incurred or to be incurred in the establishment or administration of the scheme or system under which the licence is issued`
#ASSERT `expenditure is relevant to the scheme or system under which the licence is issued` `expenditure incurred or to be incurred in respect of matters to which the licence relates`
#ASSERT NOT (`expenditure is relevant to the scheme or system under which the licence is issued` `any other expenditure`)
#ASSERT `a power to prescribe a fee allows it to recover the expenditure` `a fee for a licence` `any other expenditure` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a power to prescribe a fee allows it to recover the expenditure` `a fee for, or in relation to, the issue of a licence` `expenditure incurred or to be incurred in respect of matters to which the licence relates` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a power to prescribe a fee allows it to recover the expenditure` `a fee payable on an application for the issue of a licence` `expenditure incurred or to be incurred in the establishment or administration of the scheme or system under which the licence is issued` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a power to prescribe a fee allows it to recover the expenditure` `some other fee` `any other expenditure` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `it is within the meaning of the word in section 45A` `a charge, for the word fee` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `it is within the meaning of the word in section 45A` `to grant, give or renew, for the word issue` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `it is within the meaning of the word in section 45A` `a registration, right, permit, authority, approval or exemption, for the word licence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `it is within the meaning of the word in section 45A` `something else` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 46.
#ASSERT `the reference includes subsidiary legislation made under it` `a written law` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the reference includes subsidiary legislation made under it` `this Act, as referred to in an Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the reference includes subsidiary legislation made under it` `an Imperial Act or a Commonwealth Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the reference includes subsidiary legislation made under it` `something that is not a written law, an Imperial Act or a Commonwealth Act` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 47.
#ASSERT `the act is deemed done under the written law under which the subsidiary legislation was made` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the act is deemed done under the written law under which the subsidiary legislation was made` FALSE)
